      "writtenOn": "2024-09-18T13:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Honestly, it seems like a shame to add these to user-visible examples just to work around quirks in our build infrastructure\n\nUsers are expected to just copy paste code from examples, and having these build constraints will be confusing",
      "revId": "4dd31af4cf766f38618ccd87c1fc84907032113c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5facd39_94b723ae",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 30696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-18T13:30:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are just examples, after all. We don\u0027t run them - only verify that they build\n\nWould it be reasonable to configure our builders to build examples just on the 64-bit linux builders and nothing else?",
      "parentUuid": "1f94897e_30ad6f09",
      "revId": "4dd31af4cf766f38618ccd87c1fc84907032113c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f5a4c03_9a0c262b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 6005
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-18T13:58:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, let\u0027s do it on the builder side then. This does mean a user trying to build the example on a 32-bit port will get a build error in a dependency, but that seems like the less bad trade-off.\n\nWill soon mail https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/q/I4e1eecbb21b4a4cc2b010dad7cef47453c9f589f to opt this out of compile-only testing on 32-bit ports.",
      "parentUuid": "b5facd39_94b723ae",
      "revId": "4dd31af4cf766f38618ccd87c1fc84907032113c",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
